# Line endings.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites every file to
# CRLF on checkout. Oxfmt only accepts LF, so on a Windows machine the two fight
# each other: `ultracite fix` writes LF, git writes CRLF back, and
# `ultracite check` reports every file in the repository as unformatted forever.
#
# `eol=lf` settles it. Attributes outrank config, so the working tree gets LF on
# every machine regardless of how anyone's git is set up, and the check means
# something again.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries must never be line-ending normalised. The PDFs are course handouts and
# submitted evidence; rewriting a byte in one would corrupt it silently.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
